# Verdict

### Exact

For an \(n\)-state latent Markov process,

\[
\boxed{
\delta(\text{best null experiment},E_{t:\infty})
\le
\left(1-\frac1n\right)
\prod_{s<t}\eta(T_s).
}
\]

The bound is sharp.

### Meaning

The entire infinite future cannot recover initial-state decision information that latent mixing has already destroyed.

### Boundary

The theorem is ex ante.

A history-adaptive stopping theorem requires conditional/filter stability and is the next research target.
